what's going on guys this is rob and  we're probably a little bit late on this  upload but today is our beyond omega  level series where we break down those  powerful characters and comics and since  doctor strange came out already  naturally we have to cover him but as  powerful as the mcu version of doctor  strange is he pales in comparison to his  power level in the comics which is  normally the case with the movies versus  the comics and so for this video we're  specifically talking about doctor  strange as he was depicted prior to  having his power reduced in 2009. so if  you hear anyone talking about what's  referred to as pre-retcon doctor strange  or classic doctor strange this is the  version we're talking about so doctor  strange was created by stan lee and  steve ditko and first appeared in  strange tales number 110 in 1963. now  most of you are probably familiar with  his origin but if not stephen strange  was a skilled but arrogant surgeon whose  career was destroyed when he was in a  car accident that shatters the bones in  his hands and leaves him with nerve  damage so severe that he can no longer  perform surgery now desperate to get his  career back doctor strange begins a  quest to find any possible means to  repair his hands but this leads him to  spend all of the vast fortune he's made  over his medical career leaving him  destitute and no closer to repairing his  hands everything changes when he  overhears a conversation about a  mysterious man known as the ancient one  who lives in the himalayas and has vast  healing powers so stephen of course  seeks out the ancient one who initially  refuses to heal him because of his  hubris but after strange humbles himself  and agrees to become his disciple the  ancient one begins training him in the  mystic arts now over the years strange  would become sorcerer supreme of earth  and would continue becoming more and  more powerful until he relinquished the  title of sorcerer supreme and brian  michael bendis's new avengers number 54.  now since that time doctor strange has  regained the mantle of sorcerer supreme  but his power has not come close to the  level it was prior to him being  retconned now like many of the  characters we cover on this series  coming up with a list of powers for  doctor strange is difficult because his  only real power is his skill in  performing magic spells and using  magical artifacts however because he is  so adept at magic he's able to do a wide  variety of things and this version of  doctor strange is so powerful that he  could basically do anything he wants  hence why marvel decided to nerf his  power level later on but a partial list  of his abilities would include flight  time travel protective shields astral  projection telepathy telekinesis blasts  of mystical energy and teleportation but  as we often do i think the best way to  get an idea of how powerful classic  doctor strange was is to discuss some of  his more impressive feats so in one  instance a sorcerer named stigero had  basically been transformed into a living  start and doctor strange caused the star  to collapse into a black hole and throws  it into the cosmic wheel of change which  is basically just a plot device that was  created by the in-betweener to reshape  the universe but the takeaway point here  is that doctor strange was able to  survive being in close proximity to a  star which is an impressive feat in and  of itself but not only was he able to do  that he was also able to create a black  hole and then destroy it now speaking of  the in-betweener if you're not familiar  with him he's a cosmic abstract in the  marvel universe that represents the  concept of duality and is capable of  high level reality warping and if you  want to know more i do have a biondo  mega level video about him that you can  always check out but regardless at one  point doctor strange finds himself  trapped in the in-betweener's reality  warping and is subjected to intense  mental torture which eventually drives  him insane however he eventually breaks  free of the in-betweener's grasp by  summoning the cosmic abstracts of lord  chaos and master order defeating the  in-betweener and then imprisoning him so  here we end up seeing doctor strange  operating on the level of cosmic  entities which places him extremely high  on the power hierarchy of marvel comics  as these entities represent the concepts  that hold the universe together now  shortly after this he's able to change  the direction of the wheel of change  which undid all the changes to the  universe the in-betweener had brought  about so this basically represents  doctor strange being able to alter the  history and fabric of the universe in  another instance doctor strange  interacts with the beyonder in both  pre-retcon and post-retcon forms with  his pre-retcon version being vastly more  powerful and able to manipulate matter  and warp reality to the point that he  could destroy entire universes with a  single thought now when the two interact  doctor strange creates a veil of  illusion that traps the beyonder until  doctor strange frees him from it and he  remarks that he could have left him in  the illusion for all of eternity if he  wished and this statement is verified by  the beyonder himself furthermore dr  strange is able to undo the reality  warping the beyonder had done meaning  that he himself possesses vast reality  warping powers and as we've seen over  the course of this series once we  establish that a character can alter  reality we know they're way beyond omega  level as there's basically nothing  outside of their capabilities doctor  strange's list defeats do not end there  when confronted by the living tribunal  who is widely considered to be the  second most powerful regularly occurring  character in marvel comics only being  surpassed in power by the one above all  dr strange encountered this guy and the  living tribunal trapped him within a  spell called the roving rings of ragador  which he proclaimed no sorcerer could  escape but dr strange breaks the spell  with the greatest of ease much to the  surprise of the living tribunal who  remarks that he'd never seen it done  before and finally doctor strange had  faced the concept of death itself unites  with the cosmic entity eternity and in  doing so gets over his fear of death and  therefore becomes death meaning that he  will no longer age and is effectively  immortal unless killed in battle now  there are nearly countless examples of  classic dr strange's powers but some  others that we haven't mentioned yet  include negating the cosmic winds that  were strong enough to topple planets  from their orbits and he's been able to  defeat ridiculously powerful beings like  dormammu and nightmare in their own  realms where they're basically  omnipotent he's also defeated  shumagorath who's another nearly  omnipotent being that's conquered entire  universes in the multiverse i also have  beyond omega level videos on dormammu  nightmare and schumer gorath if you want  to learn more about why being able to  beat those three guys is a testament to  how insanely powerful dr strange was at  his peak but yeah living forever never  aging well living forever until he died  summoning cosmic entities and warping  reality classic doctor strange was a  ridiculously overpowered and well beyond  omega level character and of course i  know that there are a lot of feats that  i didn't list here but i tried to go  over the most impressive and really what  else can you add to make him seem more  powerful than this i don't really know  you know what let me know post it down  in the comments section  but with that being said guys we're  gonna bring this to an end thank you all  for watching and i will catch you all  later  peace  you
 

